<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n37514" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">praedĭcātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		1. praedico. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> In gen.,
				<i>one who makes a thing publicly known</i>, <i>a proclaimer</i>, <i>publisher</i>,
				<i>crier</i> (postclass.),
				<i><span class="en">App. M. 6, p. 176,
			4</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			In partic. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b>
			<i>One who publicly commends a thing</i>, <i>a praiser</i>, <i>eulogist</i>
			(class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">beneficii,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic.
					Balb. 2, 4</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">te ipso praedicatore ac teste,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Fam. 1, 9, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 7, 33,
			2</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b> In
			eccl. Lat., <i>a preacher</i>,
				<i><span class="en">Tert. adv. Marc. 4, 28 <i>med.</i></span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">gentium (cf. Paul),</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sulp. Sev. Ep. 1, 6</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Vulg. 1 Tim. 2, 7</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
